{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "label": "Logger (Interface)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "debug/info/warn/error plus withSource und withFields; Aufrufe unter dem Level emittieren nichts, aber die Argumente werden trotzdem evaluiert - teure Payloads brauchen einen manuellen Level-Guard."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "label": "displayName()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein Pfad ist eine Adresse, kein Name. Der Name kommt dazu, ersetzt nichts (source bleibt der Pfad) und ist ein Label fuer Menschen, nie eine Identitaet - Metriken, Tracing, Dead Letters und Wire-Identifier nutzen weiter den Pfad. Wird pro Log-Aufruf aufgeloest; wirft er, faellt der Logger auf den Pfad zurueck und warnt einmal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "label": "JsonLogger", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein newline-terminiertes JSON-Objekt pro Record nach stdout - die richtige Pipe fuer Docker-Logging-Driver, K8s-Scraper, vector, fluent-bit und jq. Errors werden als {name,message,stack} serialisiert statt als leeres Objekt; Zyklen, BigInt und Funktionen werden sanitiert, damit ein Log-Call nie wirft."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_otellogger", "label": "otelLogger", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bruecke in die OTel-Logs-API; @opentelemetry/api-logs ist optionale Peer-Dep - das Framework importiert sie nie, der Aufrufer bringt seinen Namespace-Import mit. traceId/spanId des aktiven Spans werden automatisch verlinkt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "label": "withFields (statische Felder)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gibt einen neuen Logger mit eingestempelten Feldern zurueck; in preStart binden, nicht im Feld-Initializer - this.context ist erst verfuegbar, wenn der Actor attached ist."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "label": "LogContext (MDC)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mit AsyncLocalStorage unterlegt; Werte sind nur string|number|boolean, typerzwungen, weil der Kontext ueber Cluster-Hops zu JSON serialisiert und beliebige Objekte nicht sicher round-trippen. get() liefert den lebenden Readonly-Kontext, snapshot() bei jedem Aufruf eine frische Kopie fuer Grenzen. Statisch und dynamisch mergen zur Emit-Zeit, dynamisch gewinnt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runfresh", "label": "LogContext.runFresh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fuer Arbeit, die niemandem gehoert (Hintergrundschleife, Wartungslauf, roher setTimeout-Retry). Umkehrung von with(): startet bewusst leer, schlaegt sicher fehl - ein Feld, das niemand gesetzt hat, kann nicht lecken. Das .catch ist Pflicht, unbehandelte Rejections sind auf Node seit v15 standardmaessig fatal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runeach", "label": "LogContext.runEach", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fuer gemischte Batches: Kontext jedes Items beim Einreihen snapshotten, beim Drainen wieder einspielen. Sequenziell, ein Scope pro Item, umgebender Kontext wird ignoriert statt gemerged; liefert Promise<void>, damit es nicht wie Promise.all als Nebenlaeufigkeits-Helfer gelesen wird. Ein Fehler propagiert sofort - ihn zu schlucken waere eine Supervision-Entscheidung."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontextentry", "label": "LogContextEntry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exportiert, weil eine Queue, die ihre Fuellrunde ueberlebt, einen Typ fuer {context,item} braucht."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "label": "MDC-Propagation ueber tell und Cluster-Hops", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Runtime snapshotet den Kontext auf das Envelope; der Empfaenger laeuft unter einem frischen run() dieses Snapshots, ueber Nodes hinweg reitet er auf dem Wire-Envelope - so fuegt eine correlationId einen Multi-Actor-, Multi-Node-Request zu einem durchsuchbaren Thread zusammen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_framework_clears_mdc", "label": "Der Kontext gehoert zum Envelope, nicht zur Async-Ressource", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine Auslieferung traegt den Kontext ihres tell oder keinen - nie den, der zufaellig im Timer, Socket-Callback oder Dispatcher-Tick ambient war. ReceiveTimeout, timers-Ticks, jeder Scheduler-Zeitplan, preStart/postStop und kontextlose Cluster-Frames laufen mit geleerter MDC. Vorher nagelte ein setInterval aus dem Request von Tenant A dessen Identifier an jeden spaeteren Tick und an alle, die der Tick anschrieb."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "label": "Aufgeschobene Arbeit und Tenant-Isolation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AsyncLocalStorage bindet den Store bei Erzeugung der Ressource - der Fehlerfall ist Erben, nicht Verlust. Dient die aufgeschobene Arbeit einem anderen Prinzipal als die ausloesende Runde, reisen die Identifier des einen Tenants mit den Nachrichten eines anderen: ein Datenleck, nicht bloss eine verwirrende Log-Zeile."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_consolesink", "label": "ConsoleSink / Multi-Sink-Logging", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein Logger schreibt an ein Ziel; fuer denselben Record an mehreren Stellen mit je eigenem Mindest-Level ist withLogSinks der Weg - alles andere (this.log, Level, withFields, MDC) verhaelt sich gleich."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_loglevel", "label": "LogLevel", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fuenf Level debug/info/warn/error/off, Default info; setzbar via ActorSystemOptions.withLogLevel oder actor-ts.logger.level in application.conf."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_otellogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_framework_clears_mdc", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_framework_clears_mdc", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runfresh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runeach", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runeach", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontextentry", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runfresh", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_runeach", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_loglevel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_consolesink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_framework_clears_mdc", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_receive_timeout_receivetimeout", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_framework_clears_mdc", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_timers_and_scheduling_timerscheduler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_tenant_isolation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_response_cache_auth_leak", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "